#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_square_free

#% text
# `is_square_free(n)` gives `true` when no square of a prime divides the integer `n`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# 1 is square-free. The test factors `n`.

#% item
# `is_square_free` is listable.

#% item
# For a polynomial, `is_square_free(p)` is true when no square of a nonconstant polynomial divides `p` (the gcd of `p` and each derivative is constant); `is_square_free(p, x)` looks at the variable `x` only, and `modulus: m` works modulo a prime. The integer content is not looked at.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_square_free(30)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_square_free(12)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
is_square_free(1)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_square_free(range(10))
#% output
#= [true, true, true, false, true, true, true, false, false, true]

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The density of square-free numbers is `6/pi^2`:

#% cell
n(count_if(range(10000), is_square_free)/10000)
#% output
#= 0.6083

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Square-free exactly where `moebius_mu` is not 0:

#% cell
table(moebius_mu(k) != 0, k, 10) == is_square_free(range(10))
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `moebius_mu`, `factor_integer`, `factor_square_free`
